From: John Morkel <john@morkel.me>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:03:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: add a PON mode for GDM2

When the devicetree marks GDM2 airoha,pon, the port is the SoC's PON
interface. It then:

- has no phylink instance: its carrier is what the PON MAC driver
  reports, and the link settings ethtool calls return -EOPNOTSUPP;
- uses the WAN QDMA, and refuses to probe without it;
- passes frames of 60 to 2000 bytes, enables GDM2 RX channels 0 and 1
  while it runs, and enables the TX channel of every open T-CONT;
- leaves ETS and HTB offload to the PON MAC driver, which schedules the
  T-CONTs through the interface below.

A PON MAC driver takes the port with airoha_pon_get() on the GMAC port's
devicetree node; a device link makes the frame engine driver unbind it
first. Through include/linux/soc/airoha/airoha_pon.h it then
installs its callbacks, replaces the GEM port table (each upstream GEM
port with its T-CONT and the queue of that T-CONT it uses) and the
upstream (VLAN ID, PCP) classification rules, opens and closes T-CONTs
(a T-CONT is one of the 32 QDMA channels: opening it opens its eight
queues and its GDM2 TX channel), sets a T-CONT's scheduler and rate
limit, reads its packet counters, and turns the carrier on and off. Both
tables are replaced as a whole under RCU, so the datapath reads them
without a lock; it does so in the patches that follow.

Signed-off-by: John Morkel <john@morkel.me>
---
